Sorts the elements of the input tensor along its first dimension in ascending order by value. Note torch.msort(t) is equivalent to torch.sort(t, dim=0)[0]. See also torch.sort(). Parameters input (Tensor)  the input tensor. Keyword Arguments out (Tensor, optional)  the output tensor. Example: >>> t = torch.randn(3, 4) >>> t tensor([[-0.1321, 0.4370, -1.2631, -1.1289], [-2.0527, -1.1250, 0.2275, 0.3077], [-0.0881, -0.1259, -0.5495, 1.0284]]) >>> torch.msort(t) tensor([[-2.0527, -1.1250, -1.2631, -1.1289], [-0.1321, -0.1259, -0.5495, 0.3077], [-0.0881, 0.4370, 0.2275, 1.0284]])
